{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"stdo_q05","tool":"source.read","arguments":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"q05-handoff3-reviewer-result-algebra-1","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"standards/ACTIVATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[938,1055]},"sha256":"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d"},"encoding":"utf8"}},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:8660154e94ed2d5c9bb128d467c806dea998075a25548e11868c5e4c6c5a9efe\",\"sha256\":\"8660154e94ed2d5c9bb128d467c806dea998075a25548e11868c5e4c6c5a9efe\"},\"id\":\"q05-handoff3-reviewer-result-algebra-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=eb43ad8f4c35d38d180472a21fa325a0fb99acd9cf361dd3f3258c72ea00b17b]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"## 3. Step results and disposition\\n\\nA step returns its results in the core algebra of\\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results): each evaluation it\\nperformed returns one core value with its predicate and domain outcome,\\nand an evaluation it did not perform has no result. The outcomes of\\nadmitting and activating a step, and the step's own outcomes, answer other\\nquestions than its evaluations do. This section owns them as five\\nrefinements of the core. Each names the question it answers and the\\npredicate its mapping is for, and maps each of its values to exactly one\\ncore value; the predicate travels with the value, so no refinement's\\n`satisfied` counts toward another predicate\\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results)).\\nPurpose and material relation: admission, work, decisions and effects\\nstand in the one core (P5, P6), so a consumer that combines them cannot\\nread a refused activation as a step's stop, availability as fitness or\\nacceptance, a carried ambiguity as resolved, or an unknown effect as none.\\n\\n| Refinement | Question | Predicate of the mapping |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| admission and activation | may the step begin | the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact subject and basis |\\n| construction availability | did the step yield its output | a candidate is available |\\n| disposition | what the decision owner does with an assessed candidate | the candidate is accepted at its declared boundary |\\n| ambiguity outcome | what happened to a declared ambiguity | the declared ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis |\\n| effects | did an intended external effect occur | the intended effect occurred |\\n\\nA profile that refines these values for its own units maps each of its\\nvalues to exactly one core value under FOUNDATIONS §4 Results and adds no\\ncore value.\\n\\n### Admission and activation\\n\\nA step exists only after its contract is admitted (§1, Admission) and its\\nframe is activated on the exact subject and basis (§2). The outcomes of\\nadmission and of context construction are owned here; each maps for the\\npredicate \\\"the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact\\nsubject and basis\\\", and its cause selects its value (P5, P6; RF-005 for\\nthe basis causes). The outcomes of frame activation are the `activate`\\nrefinement of [REFERENCE_FRAME §5](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#5-method-functions),\\nwhich owns their causes, their predicate and their core values. Because\\nthis predicate requires activation, a refused activation decides it with\\nthe value REFERENCE_FRAME §5 gives; the table names those outcomes and\\nmaps none of them again:\\n\\n| Outcome | Cause | Core value |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `activated` | the contract is admitted with its admission evidence (§1), Z, R, the required-edge semantics, the basis and the scope are exact and the material closure is finite and unique (§2, step 1), its projection returns a selected context (§2, step 2), and activation returns `activated_frame` | satisfied |\\n| `admission_refused(authority)` | the work authority the step needs is not admitted: no admission mechanism or explicit human override admits the exact contract, or no durable result and evidence surface is authorised and available; the outcome names the missing authority or surface and its owner | out_of_frame |\\n| `admission_refused(basis)` | the contract's cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis, or the exact subject and basis it names, cannot support it; the outcome names that basis | invalid_basis |\\n| `closure_unresolved` | the seed set Z, the relation family R, the required-edge semantics, the basis or the scope is not exact, or the material closure is not finite and unique on the exact basis (§2, step 1; AC-010), or the projection of the closure returns a gap or refusal (§2, step 2; AC-011); the outcome names the condition that fails and the basis coordinates that leave it open | invalid_basis |\\n| `out_of_frame` | no available frame and actor pairing declares a material relation or capability the evaluation needs (§2, Activation), or no fit option of §2 step 3 fits the selected context to an actor's envelope | out_of_frame |\\n| `activation_refusal` with its cause | a cause REFERENCE_FRAME §5 states | the core value REFERENCE_FRAME §5 maps that cause to |\\n\\nThese outcomes are not values of construction availability and are not\\nresults of a step. A refused admission or activation creates no step, no\\nactivation of the step's frame and no work result, the closed output of a\\nconstructing actor to its consumer; the outcome returns to the assigning\\nauthority or the declared result carrier, and no consumer records it as a\\nstep's stop state. [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §5](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#work-result)\\napplies this rule to the Worker.\\nPurpose and material relation: a mismatch known before the step begins is\\nreported with its cause in the one core, so it is neither mistaken for a\\nstep that stopped nor for one that ran.\\n\\n### Construction availability\\n\\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\\n\\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\\n\\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\\n\\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\\n\\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never\\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\\n(P5, P6).\\n\\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\\nP3).\\n\\n### Disposition\\n\\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[938,1055]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"e48f2a259dbba6f80bd2b59c0a54a0fd9d175c250bfac56e571f45ee6080bb90\",\"size_bytes\":8227,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[938,1055]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}],"structured_content":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:8660154e94ed2d5c9bb128d467c806dea998075a25548e11868c5e4c6c5a9efe","sha256":"8660154e94ed2d5c9bb128d467c806dea998075a25548e11868c5e4c6c5a9efe"},"id":"q05-handoff3-reviewer-result-algebra-1","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=eb43ad8f4c35d38d180472a21fa325a0fb99acd9cf361dd3f3258c72ea00b17b]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"## 3. Step results and disposition\n\nA step returns its results in the core algebra of\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results): each evaluation it\nperformed returns one core value with its predicate and domain outcome,\nand an evaluation it did not perform has no result. The outcomes of\nadmitting and activating a step, and the step's own outcomes, answer other\nquestions than its evaluations do. This section owns them as five\nrefinements of the core. Each names the question it answers and the\npredicate its mapping is for, and maps each of its values to exactly one\ncore value; the predicate travels with the value, so no refinement's\n`satisfied` counts toward another predicate\n([FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results)).\nPurpose and material relation: admission, work, decisions and effects\nstand in the one core (P5, P6), so a consumer that combines them cannot\nread a refused activation as a step's stop, availability as fitness or\nacceptance, a carried ambiguity as resolved, or an unknown effect as none.\n\n| Refinement | Question | Predicate of the mapping |\n|---|---|---|\n| admission and activation | may the step begin | the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact subject and basis |\n| construction availability | did the step yield its output | a candidate is available |\n| disposition | what the decision owner does with an assessed candidate | the candidate is accepted at its declared boundary |\n| ambiguity outcome | what happened to a declared ambiguity | the declared ambiguity is resolved on the exact basis |\n| effects | did an intended external effect occur | the intended effect occurred |\n\nA profile that refines these values for its own units maps each of its\nvalues to exactly one core value under FOUNDATIONS §4 Results and adds no\ncore value.\n\n### Admission and activation\n\nA step exists only after its contract is admitted (§1, Admission) and its\nframe is activated on the exact subject and basis (§2). The outcomes of\nadmission and of context construction are owned here; each maps for the\npredicate \"the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact\nsubject and basis\", and its cause selects its value (P5, P6; RF-005 for\nthe basis causes). The outcomes of frame activation are the `activate`\nrefinement of [REFERENCE_FRAME §5](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#5-method-functions),\nwhich owns their causes, their predicate and their core values. Because\nthis predicate requires activation, a refused activation decides it with\nthe value REFERENCE_FRAME §5 gives; the table names those outcomes and\nmaps none of them again:\n\n| Outcome | Cause | Core value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `activated` | the contract is admitted with its admission evidence (§1), Z, R, the required-edge semantics, the basis and the scope are exact and the material closure is finite and unique (§2, step 1), its projection returns a selected context (§2, step 2), and activation returns `activated_frame` | satisfied |\n| `admission_refused(authority)` | the work authority the step needs is not admitted: no admission mechanism or explicit human override admits the exact contract, or no durable result and evidence surface is authorised and available; the outcome names the missing authority or surface and its owner | out_of_frame |\n| `admission_refused(basis)` | the contract's cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis, or the exact subject and basis it names, cannot support it; the outcome names that basis | invalid_basis |\n| `closure_unresolved` | the seed set Z, the relation family R, the required-edge semantics, the basis or the scope is not exact, or the material closure is not finite and unique on the exact basis (§2, step 1; AC-010), or the projection of the closure returns a gap or refusal (§2, step 2; AC-011); the outcome names the condition that fails and the basis coordinates that leave it open | invalid_basis |\n| `out_of_frame` | no available frame and actor pairing declares a material relation or capability the evaluation needs (§2, Activation), or no fit option of §2 step 3 fits the selected context to an actor's envelope | out_of_frame |\n| `activation_refusal` with its cause | a cause REFERENCE_FRAME §5 states | the core value REFERENCE_FRAME §5 maps that cause to |\n\nThese outcomes are not values of construction availability and are not\nresults of a step. A refused admission or activation creates no step, no\nactivation of the step's frame and no work result, the closed output of a\nconstructing actor to its consumer; the outcome returns to the assigning\nauthority or the declared result carrier, and no consumer records it as a\nstep's stop state. [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §5](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#work-result)\napplies this rule to the Worker.\nPurpose and material relation: a mismatch known before the step begins is\nreported with its cause in the one core, so it is neither mistaken for a\nstep that stopped nor for one that ran.\n\n### Construction availability\n\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\nexists (P5, P6):\n\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\n|---|---|---|\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\n\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\n\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\n\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \"a candidate is available\", never\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\n(P5, P6).\n\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\n(P6).\n\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\nP3).\n\n### Disposition\n\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\n","coordinates":{"lines":[938,1055]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d","selected_sha256":"e48f2a259dbba6f80bd2b59c0a54a0fd9d175c250bfac56e571f45ee6080bb90","size_bytes":8227,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"standards/ACTIVATION.md","root":"method","selector":{"lines":[938,1055]},"sha256":"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1\",\n  \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:codex:handoff:3:reviewer-return\",\n  \"frame\": {\n    \"id\": \"qualification.q05.reviewer\",\n    \"revision\": \"1\"\n  },\n  \"activation\": {\n    \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:codex:handoff:3:reviewer:activation:1\",\n    \"sha256\": \"f7378d0b787d1277e671dfbc47f6470621ecddd59b48b12c12f58e82abb295b4\"\n  },\n  \"subject\": {\n    \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:codex:handoff:3:reviewer-subject\",\n    \"sha256\": \"a31fa1c00cf19183cb92cb05339db6a4e0b51afb1d47b3c362ced081199c4cb3\"\n  },\n  \"basis\": {\n    \"method_profile\": {\n      \"id\": \"urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1\",\n      \"sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"\n    },\n    \"observations\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"sha256:645b5bffe0112db95112aaea33f32cc8be3b035fb6837c88f45b1e5fccd5f435\",\n        \"sha256\": \"645b5bffe0112db95112aaea33f32cc8be3b035fb6837c88f45b1e5fccd5f435\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"actor\": {\n    \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:codex:handoff:3:reviewer\",\n    \"family\": \"openai-codex\",\n    \"authorship\": \"Fresh nonauthor Codex Reviewer; no candidate authorship\"\n  },\n  \"consumer\": \"urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:codex:handoff:3:executive\",\n  \"evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"expectation-recording\",\n      \"predicate\": {\n        \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n        \"object\": null,\n        \"path\": \"roles/PREDICATES.md\",\n        \"root\": \"control\",\n        \"selector\": null,\n        \"sha256\": \"724dee7972dc6f7429bbbd2c018ea76f4b7e05887b6f636db6a07a525ed4c1db\"\n      },\n      \"domain_outcome\": \"Required expectation recording did not complete. Governing sources were acquired before any candidate acquisition. R1/D1 determine exactly Hello, Ada. followed by one newline; R2 requires exact handoff identities, the admitted Worker operation and single-output scope evidence. The prescribed initial review.prepare expectation call returned refused(constraint), contract_violation, result=null. The bound independence document lacks allowed_family_pairs, authority_source, claim_scope, id, mechanical_sharing, predicates, require_non_author and source_first; family_limit and policy were reported as unknown fields. Operation evidence contains no acquisitions. No expectation ArtifactRef was produced, so the dependent recording call was not attempted. This finding concerns expectation recording only.\",\n      \"core_value\": \"falsified\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"sha256:d63e792dccb1e9c591650ac140dff639eadd2ac9b27728854302b39ccdf3e03f\",\n          \"sha256\": \"d63e792dccb1e9c591650ac140dff639eadd2ac9b27728854302b39ccdf3e03f\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n          \"object\": null,\n          \"path\": \"roles/INDEPENDENCE.json\",\n          \"root\": \"control\",\n          \"selector\": null,\n          \"sha256\": \"3ea82ca2183ff0b1fe9a747d0390880024ff73c1a622aa9d01aa051c31073e79\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n          \"object\": null,\n          \"path\": \"specification/REQUIREMENT.md\",\n          \"root\": \"product\",\n          \"selector\": null,\n          \"sha256\": \"2a1c18649904d1930a9f75d3102ca781c9bb0f2a40b3c572c015fdfcd08b0483\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n          \"object\": null,\n          \"path\": \"design/DESIGN.md\",\n          \"root\": \"product\",\n          \"selector\": null,\n          \"sha256\": \"1fe6e572c99a823202dbab45f27b1839cc98e665df85a601f6bc5c1d8e74c090\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n          \"object\": null,\n          \"path\": \"inputs/name.txt\",\n          \"root\": \"product\",\n          \"selector\": null,\n          \"sha256\": \"c4b7d45359e10813d1787293eb7ffa9a074e837fcf99c0281610eab5fe907e79\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"residuals\": [\n        \"No retained expectation artifact is available for the later candidate phase.\"\n      ],\n      \"invalidators\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"not_performed\": [\n    \"candidate-review\"\n  ],\n  \"work_result\": null,\n  \"residuals\": [\n    \"Root must resolve the independence-contract incompatibility and select an exact successor before re-entry, preserving this refused attempt.\",\n    \"The later same-Reviewer candidate phase requires an actual expectation ArtifactRef pinned in a new contract.\",\n    \"No greeting candidate, Worker output or Worker proof was acquired; no candidate assessment or acceptance is claimed.\",\n    \"Worker grant identity remains urn:stdo-skills:T001:q05:codex:handoff:3:worker-grant; its exercise was not assessed.\",\n    \"Cross-family semantic independence is unestablished under the declared same-family limitation.\",\n    \"Total model cost and host context size remain unknown; external/process-tree effects remain unknown.\"\n  ],\n  \"invalidators\": [\n    \"source/package drift\",\n    \"unreconciled effects\",\n    \"candidate differs from selected population\"\n  ]\n}"}}
